<header><h1>The Argent Flight</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="zeal"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Zeal">Zeal</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Argent player always votes first, even if they are the speaker.<sup>2,14</sup></li>
    <ol><li>When the Argent player is the speaker, effects timed &ldquo;after the speaker votes&rdquo;, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Bribery"><i>Bribery</i></a> action card, resolve right after the Argent player votes.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>Other players vote in their regular order after the Argent player votes; clockwise starting with the player to the left of the speaker (skipping over the Argent player as necessary).<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the Argent player abstains or otherwise casts zero votes, they cannot cast additional votes.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="raid-formation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Raid%20Formation">Raid Formation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage"><sc>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</sc></a> ability can still be used even if no fighters are present in the system.<sup>1,2,8</sup></li>
    <li><sc>Raid Formation</sc> occurs when hits are produced, not after hits are assigned. As such, canceling any hits will not prevent an opponent&rsquo;s ships from becoming damaged.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>The Argent player may choose a damaged ship. This will have no effect.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The chosen ship becomes damaged, it does not use its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability. As such, effects that trigger when a ship uses its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card, cannot be played.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> player owns their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#:~:text=Non-Euclidean%20Shielding"><i>Non&ndash;Euclidean Shielding</i></a> faction technology, this will not reduce the number of ships that the Argent player chooses.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li>The ships cannot be repaired by the effect of the <a href="/F_empyrean">Empyrean</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, the Dynamo.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Argent player plays the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Waylay"><i>Waylay</i></a> action card, hits in excess of their opponent&rsquo;s fighters will first cause chosen ships to become damaged, then those same hits must still be assigned.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>For example, say the opponent has three fighters and three dreadnoughts, undamaged. The Argent player plays <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Waylay"><i>Waylay</i></a>, and rolls five hits. This allows them to cause two of the dreadnoughts to become damaged. The opponent then has to assign all five hits. The final dreadnought may use its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability to cancel one of those hits.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If the Argent player is in combat with the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player, and the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has their mechs participating in the space combat via the effects of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>, those mechs may become damaged by the effect of <sc>Raid Formation</sc>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="strike-wing-ambuscade"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Strike%20Wing%20Ambuscade">Strike Wing Ambuscade</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="aerie-hololattice"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Aerie%20Hololattice">Aerie Hololattice</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The planet with &ldquo;<a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> 1&rdquo; is considered to be on itself for the purposes of producing ground forces.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A player with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Light/Wave_Deflector"><i>Light/Wave Deflector</i></a> technology cannot move their ships through systems containing the Argent player&rsquo;s structures, if the Argent player owns <i>Aerie Hololattice</i>.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="strike-wing-alpha"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Destroyer:~:text=Strike%20Wing%20Alpha">Strike Wing Alpha</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When a Strike Wing Alpha II rolls a 9 or 10 for their <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage"><sc>anti&ndash;fighter barrage</sc></a> ability, infantry are destroyed before any hits are canceled.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Effects that cancel hits, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Shields%20Holding"><i>Shields Holding</i></a> action card, cannot prevent the infantry from being destroyed. If an effect rerolls any anti&ndash;fighter barrage dice, the new result will determine how many infantry are destroyed.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>If the last of a player&rsquo;s ground forces are destroyed by the ability of a Strike Wing Alpha II, and that player meets the other conditions for elimination, that player is immediately eliminated. All of their units are removed from the board, and the Argent player wins the combat.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="quetzecoatl"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Flagship:~:text=Quetzecoatl">Quetzecoatl</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player may still use the <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> ability of their units against the Argent player&rsquo;s ground forces during the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step of an invasion in this system.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="trillossa-aun-mirik"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Leaders:~:text=Trillossa%20Aun%20Mirik">Trillossa Aun Mirik</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="trrakan-aun-zulok"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Leaders:~:text=Trrakan%20Aun%20Zulok">Trrakan Aun Zulok</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Ships that gain <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> due to the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Blitz"><i>Blitz</i></a> action card will contribute to the unlock condition.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Experimental%20Battlestation"><i>Experimental Battlestation</i></a> action card will not contribute.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>&ldquo;Combat&rdquo; is a unit attribute, not a unit ability.<sup>1</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="mirik-aun-sissiri"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Leaders:~:text=Mirik%20Aun%20Sissiri">Mirik Aun Sissiri</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Leaders:~:text=Helix%20Protocol">Helix Protocol</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Fighters may be moved without being transported.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Ships in systems with one of the Argent player&rsquo;s command tokens may move.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Ships may transport units out of systems that contain one of the Argent player&rsquo;s command tokens.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Ships move directly to their destination system. They may only transport units from their origin system.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li><i>Helix Protocol</i> may be used to move ships into the wormhole nexus. If the nexus is inactive, this will cause it to activate.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="aerie-sentinel"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Mech:~:text=Aerie%20Sentinel">Aerie Sentinel</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="wing-transfer"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Breakthrough:~:text=Wing%20Transfer">Wing Transfer</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Argent player performs a tactical action as normal to trigger <i>Wing Transfer</i>. They cannot move ships with <i>Wing Transfer</i> into a board state that will not be resolved, such as a system that contains other players&rsquo; ships.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>If the Argent player produces units on their turn in the active system, they will have to satisfy fleet pool and capacity limits there before they may move units to adjacent systems.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
